00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.700
Oh, and we have lots to say about it.

52
00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:51.340
We do.

53
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.180
Let's get started.

54
00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:53.940
Let's do it.

55
00:01:53.940 --> 00:02:00.200
But Dunder Mifflin Infinity part two, season four, episode four, written by Mike Schur

56
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.240
and directed by Craig Zisk.

57
00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.660
Here is a summary.

58
00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:11.120
Michael tries to show up Ryan and his emphasis on technology by winning back clients with old

59
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:14.780
fashioned customer service and elaborate gift baskets.

60
00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:21.900
Along the way, he drives into a lake after misinterpreting the directions from his GPS.

61
00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:29.360
Also in this episode, Ryan asks Pam to design some logos for Dunder Mifflin Infinity, and

62
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.080
